# User-Provided Image Assets

When the user provides an image asset and asks to use or replace it:

- Copy the original image file into the project asset folder.
- Reference that copied file directly from code.
- Do not edit, crop, resize, compress, recolor, mask, trace, redraw, convert, upscale, or otherwise process the image.
- Do not recreate the image with SVG/CSS/canvas or generated assets unless the user explicitly asks for generation or editing.
- If the requested layout needs a different size, adjust only the rendered element/container sizing in code; keep the source image file unchanged.
